  "id": "DrugBank_DB12459 - MONDO_3795",
  "verbalization": "Belotecan is associated with Ovarian Small Cell Carcinoma through a series of indirect pathways, primarily through the indication of Tretamine and Hydroxyurea. The evidence suggests that Belotecan may act as a potential therapeutic agent for ovarian cancer, as it is linked to Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary, which in turn is associated with Tretamine and Hydroxyurea, both of which are linked to Ovarian Small Cell Carcinoma. The presence of multiple indirect pathways, including the involvement of Tretamine, indicates a possible mechanism of action that could be relevant to the treatment of this cancer. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Belotecan to be repurposed in the context of ovarian small cell carcinoma, though further research is needed to establish a definitive causal relationship.",
